FactorySim is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It uses, at runtime and without redistributing them, these third-party
packages (installed by docker/Dockerfile from the ROS 2 Humble apt repositories):

- TurtleBot3 robot models and meshes (ROBOTIS, Apache-2.0): turtlebot3_gazebo, turtlebot3_description.
- OpenMANIPULATOR-X meshes (ROBOTIS, Apache-2.0): turtlebot3_manipulation_description. The arm's link offsets and
  joint limits in factory_sim/ros/robot.py follow open_manipulator_x.urdf.xacro.
- Nav2 / nav2_bringup (Apache-2.0 / BSD), Gazebo 11 and gazebo_ros_pkgs (Apache-2.0), ROS 2 Humble.

Robot type parameters in factory_sim/robots.py (speeds, payloads, footprints) are planning values chosen below the
published TurtleBot3 specifications; they are placeholders, not measurements.
